RED `file_impact`, currency falls back to invalidating on ANY code-SHA change — a fail-safe measured to over-trigger: 307 of 1,457 full re-reviews (21%) ran on byte-identical material, 171 from base-SHA drift alone (b902-18af-14ed-4da1). Allowing drift without re-review, and requiring file_impact universally, are both rejected; this scopes the fail-safe instead, EXTENDING ADR-0002's per-path machinery rather than adding a parallel trigger.\n\n## (a) Record the read-set inside the signed material\n\n**Source.** `usage_log.run_shape` emits `distinct_fetches`: `{\"tool\",\"target\"}` records where `fetch_target` returns the `path` arg for `read_file`/`list_directory`, the query STRING for `search_files`.\n**Normalization.** New module `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/read_set.py` reduces `distinct_fetches` to the read-set, in order:\n\n1. **Tool filter** — keep ONLY `tool == \"read_file\"`. `search_files` targets are query strings; `list_directory` targets are directories `_hash_file` cannot hash — dropped, not expanded (which would import unread files).\n2. **Root resolution** — resolve a relative target against the hash root `_hash_basis(repo_root)` (the pinned-SHA snapshot when attested, else the checkout); an absolute target is used as-is.\n3. **Containment** — `os.path.realpath`, then DROP anything not under that root (discards `../` escapes and outside-repo absolutes).\n4. **Repo-relative POSIX form** — `os.path.relpath` + `PurePath.as_posix()`, stripping `./` and collapsing `.`/`..`.\n5. **Existence filter** — DROP anything not an existing regular file. A mistyped read contributed no content, so baking `_ABSENT_HASH` would let an unrelated later file creation invalidate.\n6. **Dedupe + sort** — `./src/x.py` and `src/x.py` collapse to one; the manifest stays reproducible.\n\n**Plumbing.** `distinct_fetches` does not reach signing today: `sizing.usage_record` keeps only criteria/requests/token fields, and `_attach_plan_review_metrics` reads only `requests`. Three additive edits: `usage_record` passes it through; `pass1.aggregate_usage` unions the per-call lists (dedup on `(tool,target)`); `_attach_plan_review_metrics` unions every LLM step's, normalizes, and writes `coverage[\"read_set\"]` + `read_set_recorded`.\n\n`read_set_recorded` is set ONLY when a fetch was OBSERVED and survived normalization. An empty observation is deliberately NOT read as \"the review verifiably read nothing\": a runner reporting no fetch telemetry is indistinguishable from one that opened no files, so the stronger reading would scope fail-OPEN.\n\n**Signed record.** `build_manifest` gains sorted `read-path: <path>` lines plus a `read-set: <count>` marker, emitted only when recorded. The signature binds the whole manifest, so a modified read-set fails verification → `verdict=\"unsigned\"` → invalidate.\n\n## (b) Feed the read-set into the ADR-0002 dependency set\n\nScoping applies ONLY where ADR 0002 leaves a hole — all four must hold: the pre-existing set (declared `file_impact` ∪ cited paths ∪ inherited child impact) is EMPTY; the container poison rule is NOT in effect; the ticket's scope is UNDECLARED (not an authenticated `none`); a read-set was recorded. Then `dependency_hashes` composes **read-set ∪ expanded blast-radius entries** with the SAME machinery. The re-hash loop's STRUCTURE is unchanged — it still iterates exactly the entries recorded at signing — but each entry now DISPATCHES (below).\n\nEach precondition is load-bearing. Adding the blast radius to an ALREADY-scoped set would only widen it and re-create the false positive this ticket removes (an unrelated `rebar.toml` commit would invalidate a container scoped to its child's files). A poisoned container is fail-CLOSED at whole-HEAD, since any partial scope is fail-OPEN for the child's undeclared impact. And an authenticated `none` is today fully EXEMPT from drift (`compute_validity` skips even the head check); scoping it yields a non-empty set that `classify_file_scope` reclassifies `none`→`paths`, so a previously exempt attestation would START invalidating — the opposite of the goal.\n\n**Blast radius:** `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`, `rebar.toml`, `src/rebar/llm/criteria/**`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json`, `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/*.md`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/*.yaml`. (`criteria/**` holds the threshold resolver and overlay-merge core, which change outcomes with no rubric edit.)\n\n\nBecause the check iterates recorded entries, each glob is handled two ways at ATTESTATION time:\n\n- **Expansion** — sorted `glob.glob(root_dir=base, recursive=True)`, regular files only; each match becomes an **ordinary** `dep <sha256> <path>` line, so content drift names the exact file.\n- **Membership digest** — the glob PATTERN is recorded as a dep entry whose digest is sha256 of its sorted, newline-joined match list, closing the addition/deletion blind spot: a rubric added after signing has no baked per-file hash but moves the digest; a deleted member moves both it and its own entry.\n\nBoth sides route through ONE helper, `read_set.hash_dep_entry(entry, base=...)`, dispatching on a glob metacharacter (`*`, `?`, `[`): glob → membership digest, plain path → `_hash_file` (so pre-81ca manifests re-hash byte-identically). THREE call sites convert: `dependency_hashes`, `attest._rehash`, and the INLINE `_hash_file(p, base=base)` in `compute_validity`'s DEFAULT loop — distinct from `_rehash`. Missing the third would hash a glob PATTERN as a literal filename to `_ABSENT_HASH`, mismatching the signed digest and invalidating on every claim.\n\n**Fail-safes** (each falls back to invalidate-on-any-change — empty dep set → whole-HEAD): no recorded read-set (pre-change attestation, no agentic pass, no observed fetch); verification failure, including a tampered read-set; a raise during basis resolution or expansion, which `dependency_hashes` catches and logs.\n\n## (c) Report the basis\n\n`build_manifest` records one authenticated `currency-basis: file_impact | read-set | fail-safe` line chosen at sign time. `plan_review_status` (no LLM / no network) reads it off the signed manifest; a legacy manifest without it derives `file_impact` when dep lines exist, else `fail-safe`. The `--status` text renderer prints it; JSON carries the same key. ADR 0002 gains an addendum recording the read-set field, the preconditions, the composition rule, and the membership digest.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The signed manifest records the normalized read paths when fetches were observed, is absent otherwise, and a modified read-set cannot survive verification. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"read_set\" -x -q` — pinning the field, the normalization cases (non-`read_file` dropped, `./` collapsed, outside-repo and nonexistent dropped, deduped), and tamper.\n- [x] With an otherwise-empty UNDECLARED set and a moved SHA, currency reuses the ADR-0002 content-hash check over read-set ∪ blast radius: an untouched set stays current, a touched path invalidates, a file ADDED under a glob invalidates via the membership digest, and an already-scoped, poisoned, or declared-`none` set never gains the blast radius. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"no_file_impact or blast_radius or already_scoped or poisoned or exemption\" -x -q`.\n- [x] Unverifiable read-set, pre-change attestations lacking the field, and expansion failure each fall back to invalidate-on-any-change. Verify: `... -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"fallback\" -x -q`.\n- [x] `rebar review-plan <id> --status` reports the basis (file_impact | read-set | fail-safe) in text and JSON. Verify: `... -m pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py -k \"currency_basis\" -x -q`.\n- [x] ADR 0002 documents the read-set field, composition rule, and membership digest. Verify: `grep -n \"read-set\" docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/read_set.py","reason":"read-set normalization + glob dep entries"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","reason":"read-path/read-set/currency-basis lines; dep set composition"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"sign + rehash through the shared dep-entry helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"plan_review_status currency_basis"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"distinct_fetches passthrough"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","reason":"union distinct_fetches in aggregate_usage"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py","reason":"collect read-set onto the verdict"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"--status basis line"},{"path":"docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md","reason":"addendum documenting the extended contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py","reason":"basis + fallback + normalization coverage"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0725-f099-30bf-48bf"],["relates_to","53e9-464a-cd64-43ed"],["relates_to","6d71-fc3b-40e4-4c93"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1f328f97-225e-4e21-8e0f-26aa49f5449c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"81ca-9443-3443-4d27","ticket_type":"task","title":"Scope no-file-impact SHA-drift invalidation to the review read-set and cited paths (approved design a+b)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1dda8f05-dbb2-4bd5-8474-834610d32f05","40ff2b95-7dd6-4ba0-9e34-63063f5f4a04","7bd9ac2e-8614-4c6e-bdff-944942865a8b","b5192c85-1390-4469-958e-733596d181b0","8b89ec9a-88e6-43c2-8a35-3ba595d3ee24","83884a1a-39f2-4996-9ac5-f3349666b877","6943ff9c-a473-4470-b212-eab5b0517bea","3c45a286-fda7-4e89-8529-0e2a181b4610","a9023203-c107-4faf-a59d-619b2c7fb734","5ab72dd1-66a1-4893-aaac-d09606a63263","1f328f97-225e-4e21-8e0f-26aa49f5449c","5276e1ba-7dc5-4914-b17e-0835f5f9d062","a820c06b-3cb9-434f-bc77-32dcd6757a8d","5766cf38-bffb-4645-99fa-3b61568d1d38","04e9bff7-fb96-49e0-a331-e03e369d6d73","f82ba856-5b0f-4aaa-81de-3f6649b63230","4a59b55d-d753-42ef-881f-bc80df4493be","64f3a6b5-6b49-44f2-aa2d-2c276455e993","5a22c800-64a0-4ed8-a71f-55757b28a86e","72421fe8-6558-45e4-9f89-cd54bbd58432","41e9d0e6-4391-44fa-8f08-c90766c811d2","f85f4527-b6bf-4ff0-92b3-fd395e0b6bc6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786504473861958303,"uuid":"a87f1fed-2cc9-479f-9880-3857e69207ba"}